        <pre><h1>   Exercise Name:-  (Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown)</h1></pre>
        <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>


This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates a Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown. The video highlights the back
     muscles—specifically the upper back and lats (Latissimus Dorsi, Teres Major, and Rhomboids)—in glowing
     green and blue colors, illustrating how a wide overhand grip targets upper back width and muscle
     engagement during the downward pull.

Exercise Name:Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown
 <pre>
<h3>Target Muscles:</h3>

Lats (Latissimus Dorsi), Upper Back (Teres Major, Rhomboids, Middle Trapezius)
 
<h3>Secondary Muscles:</h3>

 Biceps (Biceps Brachii), Rear Deltoids, Forearms
</pre>
